  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 144 PM CDT Mon May 11 2026\n\nTonight through next Monday...\n\nA few lingering scattered showers and thunderstorms will be possible \nalong and south Hwy 84 tonight as the frontal boundary continues to \nsag south towards the Gulf. A sfc high will build over our area \nshortly after midnight which will allow for dry and quiet weather \nconditions across our CWA. Sky conditions will remain be \ngenerally cloudy across the area tonight with sky conditions \nbeginning to clear from the west early Tuesday morning. Overnight \nlows will dip into the upper 50s/lower 60s areawide. /CR/\n\nThe sfc high will keep weather conditions nice and quiet on Tuesday \nunder mostly sunny skies with daytime highs in the low 80s. Similar \nconditions is expected on Wednesday with slightly warmer \ntemperatures peaking in the mid 80s. A dry cold front will move \nacross the area on Thursday which will briefly bring afternoon highs \ndown by a few degrees. Dry conditions will continue looking ahead \ninto the weekend with highs in the upper 80s. It is possible that a \nfew areas north of Hwy 82 could see highs reach 90 degrees. Long \nterm guidance is hinting at in increase in moisture and a slight \nchance for showers/storms along and west of I-55 on Sunday. Rain",
